  "language_probability": 1.0,
  "text": "Follow the heat from a component. A cold plate transfers it into circulating equipment coolant. The warmed coolant carries that heat to a heat transfer interface. In this liquid-to-liquid example, a heat exchanger transfers energy into a separate facility coolant loop. The two fluids remain separate. The cooled equipment coolant returns to the cold plate while the facility system carries the heat onward for rejection to the environment. An alternative liquid-to-air arrangement transfers the equipment loop heat into room air. That can support some retrofits, but the room cooling system must still remove the added heat. The alternatives are not simultaneous steps in one route. A coolant distribution unit may manage circulation and heat exchange. It is not a place where heat disappears. Confirm equipment compatibility, liquid and air capacity, and the complete heat rejection path.",
